.container > * {
  padding: 10px;
  border: 2px solid rgb(95 97 110);
  border-radius: 0.5em;

  margin: 0 10px;
  flex: 1;
} To create a layout with flex items that wrap onto new rows, set the flex-wrap property on the container to wrap . Note that each flex line distributes space for that line only. Items in one line will not necessarily line up with items on other lines, as you'll see in the example below. This is why flexbox is described as one-dimensional. It is designed for controlling layout as a row or a column, but not both at the same time. html <div class="container">
